From 900b6b4255250c6efa797eafe8f5973f06fd976f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:31:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] glossary-from-source: read glossaries as a PDF prints them; a
 glossary section is never 'none'

Three defects found by the who-iris re-ingest pilot (2026-11-14):

- An L1 section prints a glossary term over definition (and an
  abbreviations list acronym over expansion); only Markdown tables and
  'term - definition' lines were read, so no row came out. stackedRows
  reads that layout, and rowsOf uses it for an L1 section when it reads
  more rows than the line readers.
- A titled section that yielded no row was dropped from the inputs, so
  the library-entry arm recorded 'none in the source' for a glossary that
  is there. It is now an input; with no term read the arm says partial.
- A title matched its glossary word anywhere: 'Step 2. Define coding
  scheme, data definitions and structures' was read as a glossary. The
  word must open the title, after a number, roman numeral or 'Annex G.'
  prefix and at most two words ('Standardized definitions', 'Key
  terms'). A control character in a title reads as a space.

Over who-iris's 211 entries: 47 change, none loses a term, 183 -> 1709
candidate terms; 3 entries with a titled section and nothing read now
report partial. Known limit: a three-column glossary (Part | Term |
Definition, 10665-75211) gives 3 of its 11 terms the Part caption as
their label; they are candidates for a person, as every row is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
